===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[pipe]], [[tube]] or [[canal]] which carries [[gas]] or [[liquid]] from one place to another
#: {{ux|en|heating and air-conditioning '''ducts'''}}
#: {{hypo|en|air duct}}
## An [[enclosure]] or [[channel]] for [[electrical]] [[cable]] [[run]]s, [[telephone]] cables, or other [[conductor]]s
##: {{hypo|en|bus duct}}
## {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[vessel]] for [[convey]]ing [[lymph]] or [[glandular]] [[secretion]]s such as [[tear]]s or [[bile]]
##: {{hypo|en|bile duct|cochlear duct|collecting duct|cystic duct|duct of Wirsung|efferent duct|ejaculatory duct|epithelial duct|lacrimal duct|milk duct|Müllerian duct|nasolacrimal duct|pancreatic duct|paramesonephric duct|tear duct|thoracic duct|thyroglossal duct|utriculosaccular duct|Wolffian duct}}
## {{lb|en|botany}} A [[tube]] or [[elongated]] [[cavity]] (such as a [[xylem]] [[vessel]]) for [[convey]]ing [[water]], [[sap]], or [[air]]
# {{lb|en|physics}} A [[layer]] (as in the [[atmosphere]] or the [[ocean]]) which occurs under usually [[abnormal]] conditions and in which [[radio wave|radio]] or [[sound wave]]s are [[confine]]d to a [[restrict]]ed [[path]]
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[guidance|Guidance]], [[direction]]
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1650|author=w:Henry Hammond|title=Of the reasonableness of Christian religion
|passage={{...}} otherwise to express His care and love to mankind, viz., in giving and consigning to them His written word for a rule and constant director of life, not leaving them to the '''duct''' of their own inclinations.}}

